msgstr "Seberapa banyak dari `overlay` yang terlihat, 0–100 (default `50`)."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`@pantoken/plugin-colors` — CSS-only color math that mirrors the InstUI `@instructure/ui-color-utils`\nhelpers (`alpha`, `darken`, `lighten`, `overlayColors`)."
msgstr "`@pantoken/plugin-colors` — matematika warna berbasis CSS saja yang mencerminkan helper InstUI `@instructure/ui-color-utils`\n(`alpha`, `darken`, `lighten`, `overlayColors`)."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "InstUI computes those at build time with `tinycolor2` against concrete hex values. pantoken emits\n`var(--instui-*)` references that resolve in the browser (often through `light-dark()`), so the\nmath has to happen in CSS instead. Each helper returns a CSS color string built from\n[`color-mix()`](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/color_value/color-mix) and\n[relative color syntax](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_colors/Relative_colors) —\nboth Baseline modern-browser features — so a single expression tracks the token even when it's a\nscheme-dependent `light-dark()` pair. Use them wherever you'd otherwise hard-code a derived shade."
msgstr "InstUI menghitung itu saat build menggunakan `tinycolor2` terhadap nilai hex konkret. pantoken mengeluarkan\nreferensi `var(--instui-*)` yang diselesaikan di browser (sering melalui `light-dark()`), jadi\nperhitungan harus terjadi di CSS. Setiap helper mengembalikan string warna CSS yang dibangun dari\n[`color-mix()`](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/color_value/color-mix) dan\n[relative color syntax](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_colors/Relative_colors) —\nkeduanya adalah fitur dasar browser modern — sehingga satu ekspresi mengikuti token bahkan ketika itu adalah\npasangan `light-dark()` yang bergantung pada skema. Gunakan mereka di mana pun Anda seharusnya meng-hardcode nuansa turunan."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/type-aliases/CssColor.md
#, no-c-format
