msgstr "The default tag prefix, mirroring the CSS layer — `&lt;instui-icon&gt;`, `.instui-button`, etc."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/DEFINITIONS.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Every element definition, in the canonical registration order. The order is load-bearing:\n`date-input` renders a nested `calendar` and `date-time-input` renders a nested `date-input`, and\nthe `ELEMENTS` tuple / the register-order test both derive from this list."
msgstr "Setiap definisi elemen, dalam urutan pendaftaran kanonis. Urutan ini memengaruhi pemuatan:\n`date-input` merender sebuah `calendar` bersarang dan `date-time-input` merender sebuah `date-input` bersarang, dan\ntuple `ELEMENTS` / tes urutan-pendaftaran keduanya diturunkan dari daftar ini."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/ELEMENTS.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The base (unprefixed) element names this package registers. [register](../functions/register.md) mints a tag per name\nunder its `prefix` option — `icon` → `<instui-icon>` by default, or `<x-icon>` for `{ prefix: \"x\" }`.\nA prefix is always applied (a custom-element name must contain a hyphen), so an empty or nullish prefix\nfalls back to the default `instui`."
msgstr "The base (unprefixed) element names this package registers. [register](../functions/register.md) mints a tag per name\nunder its `prefix` option — `icon` → `&lt;instui-icon&gt;` by default, or `&lt;x-icon&gt;` for `{ prefix: \"x\" }`.\nA prefix is always applied (a custom-element name must contain a hyphen), so an empty or nullish prefix\nfalls back to the default `instui`."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/ENGLISH_STRINGS.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "English defaults used when no locale bundle is provided."
msgstr "Default bahasa Inggris digunakan saat tidak ada bundel lokal yang disediakan."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/ICON_ELEMENTS.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Base element names that actually call [iconSvg](../functions/iconSvg.md) to render an inline glyph, as opposed to the\nseparate, CSS-only `-icon-<name>` glyph painting most components use (a mask on a CSS custom\nproperty, no JS resolution involved). `date-time-input` isn't listed because it doesn't call\n`iconSvg` itself — it nests `date-input`/`calendar` (see [NESTED\\_DEPS](NESTED_DEPS.md)), which do."
msgstr "Base element names that actually call [iconSvg](../functions/iconSvg.md) to render an inline glyph, as opposed to the\nseparate, CSS-only `-icon-&lt;name&gt;` glyph painting most components use (a mask on a CSS custom\nproperty, no JS resolution involved). `date-time-input` isn't listed because it doesn't call\n`iconSvg` itself — it nests `date-input`/`calendar` (see [NESTED\\_DEPS](NESTED_DEPS.md)), which do."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/LOCALES.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "All 44 supported locales keyed by BCP47 tag, with direction and display label."
msgstr "Semua 44 locale yang didukung dipetakan menurut tag BCP47, beserta arah dan label tampilan."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/NESTED_DEPS.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Elements whose shadow markup renders another element, so registering one requires its dependencies\ntoo: `<instui-date-time-input>` renders a `<instui-date-input>`, which renders a `<instui-calendar>`.\n[register](../functions/register.md)'s `only` filter expands through this (transitively) so a cherry-picked subset still\nworks. Keyed by base name; values are direct dependencies."
msgstr "Elements whose shadow markup renders another element, so registering one requires its dependencies\ntoo: `&lt;instui-date-time-input&gt;` renders a `&lt;instui-date-input&gt;`, which renders a `&lt;instui-calendar&gt;`.\n[register](../functions/register.md)'s `only` filter expands through this (transitively) so a cherry-picked subset still\nworks. Keyed by base name; values are direct dependencies."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/alert.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`<instui-alert>` — an inline status message with `role=\"alert\"`. The `variant` attribute maps to the\n`-color-<variant>` modifier (`info`, `success`, `warning`, `danger`). Alerts are elevated by default;\nset `has-shadow=\"false\"` to flatten one (→ `-without-shadow`, mirroring InstUI's `hasShadow={false}`).\nThe `timeout` attribute (milliseconds) auto-dismisses the alert after that delay — it fades out,\nremoves itself from the DOM, and fires a cancelable bubbling `dismiss` event (call `preventDefault()`\non it to keep the alert mounted). The fade states use `@pantoken/components`' `transition` utility;\nload its stylesheet when using timeout dismissal. Slotted content is the message body."
msgstr "`&lt;instui-alert&gt;` — an inline status message with `role=\"alert\"`. The `variant` attribute maps to the\n`-color-&lt;variant&gt;` modifier (`info`, `success`, `warning`, `danger`). Alerts are elevated by default;\nset `has-shadow=\"false\"` to flatten one (→ `-without-shadow`, mirroring InstUI's `hasShadow={false}`).\nThe `timeout` attribute (milliseconds) auto-dismisses the alert after that delay — it fades out,\nremoves itself from the DOM, and fires a cancelable bubbling `dismiss` event (call `preventDefault()`\non it to keep the alert mounted). The fade states use `@pantoken/components`' `transition` utility;\nload its stylesheet when using timeout dismissal. Slotted content is the message body."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/ar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Arabic (العربية) locale bundle."
msgstr "Bundel lokal Arab (العربية)."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/avatar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`<instui-avatar>` — a circular (or rectangular) avatar. `variant` maps to `-color-<variant>`,\n`size` to `-size-<size>`, and `shape=\"rectangle\"` to `-shape-rectangle`; slotted content is the\ninitials, or an `<img>` (use an absolute/CDN `src`) to show a photo."
msgstr "`&lt;instui-avatar&gt;` — a circular (or rectangular) avatar. `variant` maps to `-color-&lt;variant&gt;`,\n`size` to `-size-&lt;size&gt;`, and `shape=\"rectangle\"` to `-shape-rectangle`; slotted content is the\ninitials, or an `&lt;img&gt;` (use an absolute/CDN `src`) to show a photo."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/badge.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`<instui-badge>` — a small count/status badge. The `variant` attribute maps to the\n`-color-<variant>` modifier; slotted content is the count or label."
msgstr "`&lt;instui-badge&gt;` — a small count/status badge. The `variant` attribute maps to the\n`-color-&lt;variant&gt;` modifier; slotted content is the count or label."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`<instui-button>` — a token-styled `<button>`. The `variant` attribute maps to the `-color-<variant>`\nmodifier (`secondary`, `tertiary`, `success`, `danger`, `ai`, …); `margin` adds spacing around the\nhost (InstUI keywords like `small` / `medium large`); slotted content is the label."
msgstr "`&lt;instui-button&gt;` — a token-styled `&lt;button&gt;`. The `variant` attribute maps to the `-color-&lt;variant&gt;`\nmodifier (`secondary`, `tertiary`, `success`, `danger`, `ai`, …); `margin` adds spacing around the\nhost (InstUI keywords like `small` / `medium large`); slotted content is the label."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "It is also a native invoker: `popovertarget` (with optional `popovertargetaction`) toggles any\nlight-DOM `[popover]` such as `<instui-context-view>`, `<instui-popover>`, or `<instui-tray>`, and\n`command`/`commandfor` drives the command-based components (`<instui-modal>` with `--show`/`--close`,\netc.). The id is forwarded to the inner button via the invoker IDL, so it resolves across the shadow\nboundary and may point forward to an element declared later in the document."
msgstr "It is also a native invoker: `popovertarget` (with optional `popovertargetaction`) toggles any\nlight-DOM `[popover]` such as `&lt;instui-context-view&gt;`, `&lt;instui-popover&gt;`, or `&lt;instui-tray&gt;`, and\n`command`/`commandfor` drives the command-based components (`&lt;instui-modal&gt;` with `--show`/`--close`,\netc.). The id is forwarded to the inner button via the invoker IDL, so it resolves across the shadow\nboundary and may point forward to an element declared later in the document."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/ca.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Catalan (Catalá) locale bundle."
msgstr "Bundel lokal Catalan (Catalá)."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/calendar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`<instui-calendar>` — an interactive month grid. `value` (`yyyy-mm-dd`) is the selected day and\n`view` (`yyyy-mm-dd`, optional) the visible month. The prev/next chevrons and every day are\n`<button>`s driving the Invoker Commands API (`--calendar-prev`, `--calendar-next`,\n`--calendar-select`) at the grid; selecting a day updates `value`/`view` and dispatches a composed,\nbubbling `change` event (`detail.value` is the ISO date). Renders its own grid (no slot), so it\nworks standalone or nested inside a date picker."
msgstr "`&lt;instui-calendar&gt;` — an interactive month grid. `value` (`yyyy-mm-dd`) is the selected day and\n`view` (`yyyy-mm-dd`, optional) the visible month. The prev/next chevrons and every day are\n`&lt;button&gt;`s driving the Invoker Commands API (`--calendar-prev`, `--calendar-next`,\n`--calendar-select`) at the grid; selecting a day updates `value`/`view` and dispatches a composed,\nbubbling `change` event (`detail.value` is the ISO date). Renders its own grid (no slot), so it\nworks standalone or nested inside a date picker."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/contextView.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`<instui-context-view>` — a callout surface with a caret. The host itself is a native `[popover]`\n(top layer + light-dismiss), so a light-DOM `popovertarget`/`command` button can toggle it by id.\nPosition it near its trigger with CSS anchor positioning where supported; otherwise it centres in\nthe top layer. Content goes in the default slot."
msgstr "`&lt;instui-context-view&gt;` — a callout surface with a caret. The host itself is a native `[popover]`\n(top layer + light-dismiss), so a light-DOM `popovertarget`/`command` button can toggle it by id.\nPosition it near its trigger with CSS anchor positioning where supported; otherwise it centres in\nthe top layer. Content goes in the default slot."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/cy.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Welsh (Cymraeg) locale bundle."
msgstr "Bundel lokal Welsh (Cymraeg)."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/da.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Danish (Dansk) locale bundle."
msgstr "Bundel lokal Denmark (Dansk)."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/dateInput.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`<instui-date-input>` — a text field plus a calendar dropdown. The trigger toggles a `[popover]`\nthrough the built-in `toggle-popover` Invoker Command (a click fallback covers browsers without the\nAPI); picking a day in the nested `<instui-calendar>` fills the field (ISO `yyyy-mm-dd`), closes the\npopover, and emits a composed, bubbling `change` (`detail.value`). Typing a valid `yyyy-mm-dd` (or\nclearing it) and committing on the input's `change` works too. `value` is the ISO date, `label` the\naccessible name (default `Date`), and `placeholder` the hint (default `yyyy-mm-dd`)."
msgstr "`&lt;instui-date-input&gt;` — a text field plus a calendar dropdown. The trigger toggles a `[popover]`\nthrough the built-in `toggle-popover` Invoker Command (a click fallback covers browsers without the\nAPI); picking a day in the nested `&lt;instui-calendar&gt;` fills the field (ISO `yyyy-mm-dd`), closes the\npopover, and emits a composed, bubbling `change` (`detail.value`). Typing a valid `yyyy-mm-dd` (or\nclearing it) and committing on the input's `change` works too. `value` is the ISO date, `label` the\naccessible name (default `Date`), and `placeholder` the hint (default `yyyy-mm-dd`)."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/dateTimeInput.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`<instui-date-time-input>` — a nested `<instui-date-input>` plus a native time field. A change to\neither recomputes a combined `value` (`yyyy-mm-ddThh:mm`, or just the date when no time) and emits\na composed, bubbling `change` (`detail.value`). Setting `value` splits it back across the two\nfields."
msgstr "`&lt;instui-date-time-input&gt;` — a nested `&lt;instui-date-input&gt;` plus a native time field. A change to\neither recomputes a combined `value` (`yyyy-mm-ddThh:mm`, or just the date when no time) and emits\na composed, bubbling `change` (`detail.value`). Setting `value` splits it back across the two\nfields."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/de.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "German (Deutsch) locale bundle."
msgstr "Bundel lokal Jerman (Deutsch)."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/drawerLayout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`<instui-drawer-layout>` — a side tray plus main content area. The `open` attribute reveals the\ntray; `placement` (`start`|`end`) picks the side. Drivable from light DOM via Invoker Commands:\n`<button command=\"--toggle|--open|--close\" commandfor=\"drawer-id\">`. Content goes in the default\nslot; the tray in `slot=\"tray\"`. The interactions behavior auto-toggles overlay mode based on the\n`--pantoken-bp-md` threshold."
msgstr "`&lt;instui-drawer-layout&gt;` — a side tray plus main content area. The `open` attribute reveals the\ntray; `placement` (`start`|`end`) picks the side. Drivable from light DOM via Invoker Commands:\n`<button command=\"--toggle|--open|--close\" commandfor=\"drawer-id\">`. Content goes in the default\nslot; the tray in `slot=\"tray\"`. The interactions behavior auto-toggles overlay mode based on the\n`--pantoken-bp-md` threshold."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/drawerLayout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The content pane carries `role=\"region\"`, matching InstUI's DrawerLayout; label it with `aria-label`/`aria-labelledby` when the surrounding context doesn't already name it."
msgstr "Panel konten membawa `role=\"region\"`, sesuai dengan DrawerLayout InstUI; beri label dengan `aria-label`/`aria-labelledby` ketika konteks di sekitarnya belum memberinya nama."

#: renderers/web-components/src/variables/drilldown.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`<instui-drilldown>` — a stateful, multi-level menu over the menu styles. Each level is a light-DOM\n`[data-page=\"id\"]` whose inner `.item`s are cloned into a shadow `.instui-menu`; an item with\n`data-goto=\"id\"` descends to that page and a synthesized Back row (or any `[data-back]` item)\nreturns. The light DOM is the data source only — with no `<slot>` it never renders, so shadow CSS\nfully styles each panel. The `active` attribute reflects the current page and can be set to\nnavigate; a bubbling `navigate` event (`detail.page`) fires on every move. Drivable from light DOM\nvia Invoker Commands: `<button command=\"--goto\" commandfor=\"dd-id\" data-page=\"…\">` descends and\n`<button command=\"--back\" commandfor=\"dd-id\">` returns."
msgstr "`&lt;instui-drilldown&gt;` — a stateful, multi-level menu over the menu styles. Each level is a light-DOM\n`[data-page=\"id\"]` whose inner `.item`s are cloned into a shadow `.instui-menu`; an item with\n`data-goto=\"id\"` descends to that page and a synthesized Back row (or any `[data-back]` item)\nreturns. The light DOM is the data source only — with no `&lt;slot&gt;` it never renders, so shadow CSS\nfully styles each panel. The `active` attribute reflects the current page and can be set to\nnavigate; a bubbling `navigate` event (`detail.page`) fires on every move. Drivable from light DOM\nvia Invoker Commands: `<button command=\"--goto\" commandfor=\"dd-id\" data-page=\"…\">` descends and\n`<button command=\"--back\" commandfor=\"dd-id\">` returns."

